abstract: >-
  A speculative hypothesis treating the universe as a globally conserved
  informational structure, where cosmological cycles correspond to changes in
  local information readability rather than temporal restarts. Version 0.1.7
  adds a conditional arithmetic reconstruction with supplied coherent reference
  data, a stationary-state entropy obstruction in its exact simple-spectrum
  model, and an explicit failure of full operator-norm reconstruction stability.
  A fixed-access follow-up separates failure of uniform stability under an
  energy budget from local continuity conditioned on reference amplitudes.
  Selected proof components are Lean-checked, not the complete construction.
  Earlier results and core postulates are unchanged. No physical algebra
  selector, cosmological entropy functional, transition dynamics, or prediction
  is derived. Reviews and diagnostic checks are internal and AI-assisted.
